4.5 Forgotten Treasure Engine

This is the signature feature and must receive special attention.

Implement a Forgotten Treasure page that identifies neglected items.

Rules:

An item becomes eligible for forgotten status when it has not been reviewed for at least 14 days.
Use the last-reviewed timestamp if available; otherwise, use the creation timestamp.
Exclude completed and archived items.
Calculate elapsed time using actual timestamps.
Display how long each item has been neglected.
Provide actions to revisit, complete, recategorize, archive, or delete items.
Allow users to filter forgotten items by category.
Provide a "Rescue an Item" button that selects an eligible forgotten item.
Provide a "Review Now" action that updates the item's review timestamp.
Show a useful empty state when no forgotten items exist.

Do not mark every newly created item as forgotten.

Use a configurable default threshold of 14 days, with the threshold stored in application settings or a well-defined server-side configuration.

For a first-time demo, seed sample records with historical timestamps so this feature can be demonstrated immediately.

4.6 Clutter Score

Create a transparent Clutter Score ranging from 0 to 100.

Define the score as the percentage of active items requiring attention.

For the initial implementation, an active item requires attention when it is incomplete and either:

It is in the DO category; or
It has been neglected for at least 14 days.

Calculate:

Clutter Score = round(100 × attentionItems / activeItems)

Where:

activeItems excludes completed and archived records.
attentionItems contains active items satisfying the attention rules.
If there are no active items, the score is 0.

Display:

The numerical score.
A progress indicator.
The number of items requiring attention.
A short explanation of the calculation.
A suggested action based on the score.

Use a clear visual legend:

0–24: Well Organized
25–49: Light Clutter
50–74: Needs Attention
75–100: High Clutter

These labels are motivational product indicators, not scientifically validated measurements.

Use the same calculation rules everywhere. Do not generate random scores or use AI to fabricate metric values.

