11. Row Level Security (RLS) / Data Isolation Rules

Enable RLS on every user-owned table.

Items

Users may select, insert, update, and delete only their own items.

Use the authenticated identity supplied by Supabase, such as auth.uid(), to enforce ownership.

For inserts:

Require user_id = auth.uid().
Reject attempts to create records for another user.

For updates:

Verify ownership before allowing the update.
Ensure ownership cannot be changed to another user.
Use appropriate USING and WITH CHECK conditions.

For deletes:

Require ownership of the target record.
Profiles

Users may access and update only their own profile.

Do not allow users to modify privileged account fields.

User Settings

Users may access and update only their own settings.

Validate the threshold at the application and database layers.

AI Activity Logs

If implemented, users may read only their own permitted audit information.

Prevent clients from inserting arbitrary audit records that impersonate other users.

Service Role
Never expose the Supabase service-role key to the frontend.
Never disable RLS to simplify development.
Use the service-role key only in trusted server-side operations when absolutely necessary.
Prefer the authenticated user's Supabase context for ordinary database access.
Never trust a client-provided user_id as proof of ownership.
Acceptance of Isolation

Test that two different users cannot read, modify, archive, or delete each other's items, profiles, or settings.

